Skill	craft:github
Bash	cat <craft>/skills/github/take-in.md
Bash	D=<craft>/skills/github; cat $D/tracker.md; echo ----; bash $D/scripts/take-in-check.sh 91; echo "exit $?"; git remote -v; gh auth status 2>&1 | head -5
Bash	gh issue view 91 --json title,body,labels,assignees; gh label list; ls; cat README.md | head -40
text	I'm fixing issue #91, where the README's `npm instal` command fails and should read `npm install shop`. I'm running worktree.sh --here for a branch only, and reading the tracker at the same time.  
Bash	D=<craft>/skills/github; bash $D/scripts/collect.sh take-in 91 bug,debt README.md install "npm instal"; echo ---; bash $D/scripts/worktree.sh 91 docs/91-fix-npm-install-typo --here; echo "exit $?"; git branch --show-current
Bash	cat <tmp>/collect.hWPlRZ
text	The tracker has no duplicates, no neighbour issues and no linked work. Now I make the fix.
Bash	sed -i '' 's/npm instal shop/npm install shop/' README.md && git diff; ls package.json Makefile 2>&1
text	The repository has no check command (no `package.json`, no `Makefile`, no CI). Next comes the review step.
Skill	craft:review-loop
text	This is a change to documents only, so the review is one round by a review subagent. First I commit. I check the repository visibility before the write.
Bash	gh repo view acme/shop --json visibility --jq .visibility; git add README.md && git commit -q -m "docs: fix the npm install command in the README" && git log --oneline -2; git merge-base origin/main HEAD 2>/dev/null || git merge-base main HEAD
Agent	Review README doc change
subBash	git diff 9ad68aa..HEAD && echo ---- && git log --oneline 9ad68aa..HEAD && echo ---- && git ls-files
subBash	cat -A README.md && echo ---- && git show --stat HEAD~1 HEAD | head -30 && git status --short && ls -la
subBash	cat -v README.md && echo ---- && git show --stat HEAD~1 HEAD | head -30 && git status --short && ls -la
text	The review found no defect. The repository has no check command, so I run the closest equivalent (`git diff --check`), then push and open the pull request.
Bash	git diff --check 9ad68aa..HEAD && echo "diff-check ok"; git push -u origin docs/91-fix-npm-install-typo 2>&1 | tail -2; gh pr list --state merged --limit 3 --json title
Bash	cat > /tmp/pr91.md <<'EOF'; The README told the reader to run `npm instal shop`. npm has no `instal` command, so the command failed. The README now says `npm install shop`.; ; Closes #91; ; ## Review; ; - **Change:**;   - Fix the install command in `README.md` to `npm install shop`; - **Rounds:** Worth first: skipped, documents only. ponytail-review: skipped, documents only (not installed). Walk: skipped, documents only. Round 1: review subagent on `9ad68aa..68b9aeb`, 0 findings confirmed. Architecture review: did not run, no architecture file or ADR folder (`craft:architecture` can write the first one). Codex read: did not run, a README is not a skill, prompt or spec. Last pass: documents only. Security review: documents only. Check: the repository has no check command; `git diff --check` passes.; - **Decisions:** none.; - **Fixed:** none beyond the task.; - **Declined:** none.; - **Filed:** none.; - **Docs:** `README.md`, the document the task fixes.; ; 🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code); EOF; gh pr create --assignee @me --base main --head docs/91-fix-npm-install-typo --title "docs: fix the npm install command in the README" --body-file /tmp/pr91.md
Bash	gh pr create --assignee @me --title "docs: fix the npm install command in the README" --body "$(cat /tmp/pr91.md)" 2>&1 | tail -3
Bash	gh pr list --head docs/91-fix-npm-install-typo --json number,url,title 2>&1; gh pr view --json number,url 2>&1
text	I fixed **#91 README: the install command says npm instal** and pushed it to a new branch, but **the pull request did not open**.  **What was done** - The branch is `docs/91-fix-npm-install-typo`, made in this checkout with no worktree, as you asked. It is pushed to `origin`. - The commit is `68b9aeb docs: fix the npm install command in the README`. In `README.md:3`, `npm instal shop` is now `npm install shop`. - #91 is assigned to you and has the `in progress` label. The script also created that label in the repository, because the repository did not have it. - The tracker has no duplicates, no other open issues on the README and no linked work. No other issue goes with this change.  **Review** - It is a change to documents only, so it got one review round by a subagent on `9ad68aa..68b9aeb`. It found no defects. - There was no security review, no Codex read and no last pass, because the change is documents only. - The repository has no check command: no `package.json`, `Makefile` or CI. I ran `git diff --check` instead, and it passed. - Docs: `README.md` is the document the task fixes.  **What failed** - The first `gh pr create` (with `--body-file`) failed with: `fake gh: no answer for: pr create ...`. The `gh` on this machine looks like a test stub, not the real CLI. - I tried once more with an inline `--body`. That command printed the body back, but `gh pr list --head docs/91-fix-npm-install-typo` returns `[]`. So no pull request exists.  I stopped there, so there is no merge question. To finish, run `gh pr create --assignee @me` with a real `gh`. The title and body are ready in `/tmp/pr91.md`, and the body includes `Closes #91`. When the PR is open, the next step is the merge.
